  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Consider the following radioactive decay process:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mmultiscripts><mi>A</mi><mprescripts/><mn>84</mn><mn>218</mn></mmultiscripts><mover><mo>&#10230;</mo><mi>&#945;</mi></mover><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mover><mo>&#10230;</mo><msup><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></mover><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mover><mo>&#10230;</mo><mi>&#947;</mi></mover><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mover><mo>&#10230;</mo><mi>&#945;</mi></mover><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mover><mo>&#10230;</mo><msup><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mover><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mover><mo>&#10230;</mo><mi>&#947;</mi></mover><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>6</mn></msub></math></p><p>The mass number and the atomic number of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>6</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;are given by:</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>210</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>82</mn></math>",
